## Web App Guide

This is a **server-rendered HTML app** (not a JSON API). Visit `http://localhost:8080/users` in a browser to see the user list page (the port is `PORT` in `.env`, default `8080`). The list is **paginated**: when there are more users than fit on a page, a **"Next →"** link appears carrying an opaque `?cursor=…` for the following page.

### Add A New User

```text
curl --location 'http://localhost:8080/users' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \
--data-urlencode 'name=John Doe'
```

Reload `http://localhost:8080/users` to see the new user on the page.

### Update An Existing User

```text
curl --location --request PUT 'http://localhost:8080/users/<USER_ID>' \
--header 'Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded' \
--data-urlencode 'name=Jane Doe'
```

### Delete An Existing User

```text
curl --location --request DELETE 'http://localhost:8080/users/<USER_ID>'
```
{{if .Broker}}
### Events

On a write (creating a user), the app publishes an event to **{{.Broker}}**, and a consumer loop runs alongside the HTTP server. See the "Broker workflow" section of `AGENTS.md`.

**{{.Broker}} runs in a container**: start it with `make docker-up` before `make run`, or the app cannot reach the broker. `make docker-down` stops it (`make docker-down-rm-vol` also drops the volume).
{{end}}{{if .Observability}}
### Observability

`make docker-up` also starts an **OpenTelemetry Collector** (config: `configs/otel-collector.yaml`). The app exports traces and metrics to it over OTLP — see the `OTEL_*` keys in `.env`.
{{end}}